The '''Soma Prime''' is the [[Prime]] variant of the {{Weapon|Soma}} assault rifle, featuring a greater magazine size, greater ammo reserves, faster spool-up, and a slight increase to [[status chance]]. It was released alongside {{WF|Nova Prime}} and {{Weapon|Vasto Prime}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*Requires a spool-up of '''4''' shots before optimal fire rate is achieved.
**Fire rate starts at '''25%''' of the listed value, and increases by '''30%''' per shot.
*Can use the Soma Prime-exclusive {{M|Hata-Satya}} mod.

{{Advantages|name=Soma Prime|class=Rifle|trigger=Auto-Spool|}}

{{Disadvantages|name=Soma Prime|class=Rifle|trigger=Auto-Spool|
* Spool-up creates a warm-up period of weakness for fire rate, making short engagements undesirable.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Soma}}

==Acquisition==
{{PrimeTable}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

===Vaultings===
*On [https://forums.warframe.com/topic/719509-new-items-are-entering-prime-vault/ November 15th, 2016,] it was announced that Soma Prime, along with {{WF|Nova Prime}} and {{Weapon|Vasto Prime}}, would enter the [[Prime Vault]] and be retired from the reward tables on November 22nd, 2016. Any preexisting components or fully-built weapons will remain as is.
*On October 31st, 2017, Soma Prime became available for acquisition through Twitch Prime along with {{WF|Frost Prime}}. This limited time offer lasted until December 31st, 2017.
*Soma Prime, along with {{WF|Mag Prime}}, {{WF|Nova Prime}}, {{Weapon|Dakra Prime}}, {{Weapon|Boar Prime}}, and {{Weapon|Vasto Prime}}, were [https://forums.warframe.com/topic/1027106-the-prime-vault-is-open/ unvaulted] from November 13th, 2018 to January 29th, 2019.
*Soma Prime, along with {{WF|Trinity Prime}}, {{WF|Nova Prime}}, {{Weapon|Dual Kamas Prime}}, and {{Weapon|Vasto Prime}}, were [https://www.warframe.com/news/trinity-and-nova-prime-vault unvaulted] once again from May 26th, 2020 to September 29th, 2020.

== Incarnon Genesis ==
{{Transclude|Soma Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Soma Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*A critical focused build using {{M|Point Strike}}, {{M|Argon Scope}} ({{M|Galvanized Scope|Galvanized}}) and {{M|Hata-Satya}}, combined with {{M|Vital Sense}} and {{M|Bladed Rounds}}, and/or {{M|Hammer Shot}} is a valuable way to mod this weapon to take advantage of its high [[critical chance]] to increase its otherwise meager base damage.
**The critical focused build will also synergize extremely well with {{WF|Gyre}}'s {{A|Rotorswell}}, as she can keep hammering enemies with near-constant critical hits and very high rate of fire to keep her ability's chain lightning strikes triggering.
**If you are low on slots, {{M|Point Strike}}, {{M|Vital Sense}}, and {{M|Bladed Rounds}} provide the most overall increase in DPS.
*Reload time can be shortened by using a melee attack or dodge roll when the reload timer reaches about 3/4. This works because, like many older weapons, the magazine is updated at this time instead of at the end, making the remaining time extraneous.
*Due to the weapon's high rate-of-fire combined with its low base damage, the Soma Prime can be ammo inefficient. Using {{M|Vigilante Supplies}}/{{M|Rifle Ammo Mutation}} and/or {{M|Rifle Scavenger}} can be used to recover a steady supply of ammo. Alternatively, ammo can be instantly replenished using [[Squad Ammo Restore]]s. Additionally, [[Carrier]]'s {{M|Ammo Case}} mod grants more reserve ammo and turns unused ammo drops into ammo for equipped weapons.

==Trivia==
*The Soma Prime was one of the first prime items which had colorable gold parts. This trait was shared with the {{Weapon|Vasto Prime}}, {{WF|Nova Prime}} and the [[Warframe Cosmetics#Syandana|Pyra Prime Syandana]].
*The ring-like formation through which the Warframe holds the weapon with their left hand rotates while firing, making this one of the few primary weapons that have firing animations.
**Like its non-prime version, the Soma Prime's magazine passes up through its receiver as it fires, with the portion of the magazine consumed indicating the amount of ammo left.
*The Soma Prime is also the only Primed weapon in the game that keeps its original counterpart's base damage.
*[https://calamitymod.wiki.gg/wiki/Soma_Prime Soma Prime] is one of several weapons which makes an appearance in the Calamity Mod, a popular mod for the game Terraria. Other weapons which appear in the mod are {{Weapon|Rubico Prime}} and {{Weapon|Corinth Prime}}.

